  "security_implications": "The sp2v signals likely carry AES state/control values. The sp2v_sig_err signals provide glitch detection integrity. The per-instance Sp2VEnSecBuf parameter directly controls whether the buffer‑check security feature is active for each index i. If any index has EnSecBuf=0, a critical signal could be left unprotected, enabling fault injection that corrupts AES state, leaks secret material, or bypasses security checks. The type cast on sp2v_sig_chk may also hide error conditions if widths mismatch.",
